"""
Ship anti-heeling system.

Ported from `ShipSIM.Components.AntiHeelingSystem.AntiHeeling`.

The original Modelica model has:
- A hysteresis on/off controller (`OnOffController`) on `|ship_heel|` with bandwidth
  `max_angle`, feeding a `TriggeredTrapezoid` that ramps the pump flow to `Q` over 10 s.
- A `WorldTorque` applied to `frame_a` for the multibody hull.
- A fixed `time < 500 s` start-up delay forcing zero pump flow.

This Dyad port:
- Replaces the on/off + trapezoid with a smooth saturating activation
  `pump_flow = Q · clamp((|ship_heel| - max_angle/2) / max_angle, 0, 1) · ifelse(time < startup_delay, 0, 1)`.
  Same conceptual purpose: when |heel| exceeds the threshold the pump runs at full rate;
  in between the threshold and the threshold + bandwidth, it ramps linearly.
- Restores multibody coupling via a `Frame2D` connector. The 3D roll righting moment is
  mapped onto `frame_a.tau` (yaw) since 2D PlanarMechanics has only one rotational DOF.
  `M_adr` is also kept as a `RealOutput` for diagnostics; don't double-apply.
- Preserves the bounded tank moment integration `M_tks` and the saturation at `M_max`.

The internal state `M_tks` is integrated with the original equation
  `der(M_tks) = sign(ship_heel) · pump_flow / 3600 · ρ · (B - b)`.
"""
component AntiHeeling
  parameter B::Length = 24.3
  parameter b::Length = 6.35
  parameter V_tk::Real = 211.47
  parameter rho::Density = 1.025
  parameter Q::Real = 200
  "Maximum admissible heel before the pump turns on full [deg]"
  parameter max_angle::Real = 0.1
  "Startup delay before the pump may run [s] (matches upstream `time < 500`)"
  parameter startup_delay::Real = 500

  ship_heel = RealInput()
  pump_flow = RealOutput()
  M_adr = RealOutput()        # righting moment from the AH system [t·m]

  "Hull frame to apply righting yaw moment to (PlanarMechanics).
  In 2D planar mechanics, the only rotational DOF is yaw, so the upstream 3D roll
  righting moment is mapped onto frame_a.tau (yaw). For a true roll model the upstream
  3D framework is needed; this is the closest 2D analogue."
  frame_a = Frame2D()

  variable M_tks::Real         # internal moment state
  variable v_max::Real
  variable M_max::Real
  variable activation::Real
relations
  initial M_tks = 0

  v_max = V_tk * 0.40
  M_max = rho * v_max * (B - b)

  activation = ifelse(time < startup_delay, 0,
                      clamp((abs(ship_heel) - max_angle / 2) / max_angle, 0, 1))
  pump_flow = Q * activation

  der(M_tks) = ifelse(ship_heel >= 0, 1, -1) * pump_flow / 3600 * rho * (B - b)
  M_adr = ifelse(abs(M_tks) > M_max,
                 M_max * ifelse(ship_heel >= 0, 1, -1),
                 M_tks)

  # Convert M_adr (t·m) → N·m and apply to hull frame as a yaw moment (2D analogue
  # of the upstream 3D roll-axis WorldTorque). Multiply by g_n·1000 to match upstream
  # `torque.torque = {-M_adr*g_n*1000, 0, 0}`.
  frame_a.fx = 0
  frame_a.fy = 0
  frame_a.tau + (-M_adr * 9.80665 * 1000) = 0
end
